ording to the fruit of his doings:¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™which hast set signs and wonders in the land of Egypt, even unto this day, and in Israel, and among other men; and hast made thee a name, as at this day;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬and hast brought forth thy people Israel out of the land of Egypt with signs, and with wonders, and with a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with great terror;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxand hast given them this land, which thou didst swear to their fathers to give them, a land flowing with milk and honey;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÙand they came in, and possessed it; but they obeyed not thy voice, neither walked in thy law; they have done nothing of all that thou commandedst them to do: therefore thou hast caused all this evil to come upon them:¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚbehold the mounts, they are come unto the city to take it; and the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans, that fight against it, because of the sword, and of the famine, and of the pestilence: and what thou hast spoken is come to pass; and, behold, thou seest it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd thou hast said unto me, O Lord GOD, Buy thee the field for money, and take witnesses; for the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPBehold, I am the LORD, the God of all flesh: is there any thing too hard for me?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the Chaldeans, and into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and he shall take it:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñand the Chaldeans, that fight against this city, shall come and set fire on this city, and burn it with the houses, upon whose roofs they have offered incense unto Baal, and poured out drink offerings unto other gods, to provoke me to anger.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÌFor the children of Israel and the children of Judah have only done evil before me from their youth: for the children of Israel have only provoked me to anger with the work of their hands, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬For this city hath been to me as a provocation of mine anger and of my fury from the day that they built it even unto this day; that I should remove it from before my face,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙùbecause of all the evil of the children of Israel and of the children of Judah, which they have done to provoke me to anger, they, their kings, their princes, their priests, and their prophets, and the men of Judah, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥And they have turned unto me the back, and not the face: though I taught them, rising up early and teaching them, yet they have not hearkened to receive instruction.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book§chapter «first_verse"ªlast_verse#¦verses’„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWBut they set their abominations in the house, which is called by my name, to defile it.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd they built the high places of Baal, which are in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to cause their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire unto Molech; which I commanded them not, neither came it into my mind, that they should do this abomination, to cause Judah to sin.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book§chapter «first_verse$ªlast_verse&¦verses“„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÒAnd now therefore thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, concerning this city, whereof ye say, It shall be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon by the sword, and by the famine, and by the pestilence;¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÒbehold, I will gather them out of all countries, whither I have driven them in mine anger, and in my fury, and in great wrath; and I will bring them again unto this place, and I will cause them to dwell safely:¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5and they shall be my people, and I will be their God:¦layout ªlast_verse&…¤book§chapter «first_verse'ªlast_verse)¦verses“„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„and I will give them one heart, and one way, that they may fear me for ever, for the good of them, and of their children after them:¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´and I will make an everlasting covenant with them, that I will not turn away from them, to do them good; but I will put my fear in their hearts, that they shall not depart from me.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Yea, I will rejoice over them to do them good, and I will plant them in this land assuredly with my whole heart and with my whole soul.¦layout ªlast_verse)…¤book§chapter «first_verse*ªlast_verse,¦verses“„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—For thus saith the LORD; Like as I have brought all this great evil upon this people, so will I bring upon them all the good that I have promised them.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰And fields shall be bought in this land, whereof ye say, It is desolate without man or beast; it is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚSMen shall buy fields for money, and subscribe evidences, and seal them, and take witnesses in the land of Benjamin, and in the places about Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah, and in the cities of the mountains, and in the cities of the valley, and in the cities of the south: for I will cause their captivity to return, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse,